+# Team conventions
+
+## Running dbt
+
+- Build and test one model: `DBT_PROFILES_DIR=. dbt build -s <model>`.
+- Never run dbt with `--target prod` without explicit sign-off from a human.
+- If a seed changes, run `dbt seed --full-refresh`.
+- Don't run `dbt clean` without asking first — it wipes the target folder.
+- The `raw` schema is loaded from seeds; don't edit the CSVs by hand.
+
+## Project conventions
+
+- Commit messages: short, imperative.
+- Ask before adding new packages to `pyproject.toml`.
+- Finance models are owned by Bob — ask him before changing anything there.
+- If you're not sure about something, ask, don't guess.
+
+## Where things live
+
+- Directory-specific conventions live in that directory's own `AGENTS.md`
+  (see `models/`, `models/staging/`, `macros/`).
+- The step-by-step procedure for adding a model is a skill:
+  `skills/add-model/SKILL.md`.
+- Personal working style belongs in `people/<name>.md`, not here.
+
+## Precedence
+
+- When layers disagree: personal notes in `people/<name>.md` win over this
+  file, and this file wins over the defaults in directory `AGENTS.md` files.
